Dear Sirs and Mesdames,

=20

I attach for the public record Statement A =E2=80=94 Suppression of Disability Ev=
idence Across Eight Orders. The document is a horizontal forensic analysis o=
f the systematic and exhaustive suppression of my documented disability acro=
ss eight orders, judgments, and decisions handed down between 18 April 2024 =
and 7 May 2026, by six judges across three courts: the Family Division of th=
e High Court, the Court of Appeal Civil Division, and the Administrative Cou=
rt.

=20

The analytical framework is the framework I set out in my Permission to App=
eal application filed at the Court of Appeal on 22 July 2024. That applicati=
on was refused by Moylan LJ on 23 December 2024. The framework has been on t=
he formal court record for nearly two years.

=20

The mechanism documented in Statement A operates at four discrete levels:=20

=20

(a) suppression of evidence that exists on the contemporaneous court record=
;=20

(b) assertion of findings not traceable to identifiable source material wit=
hin the three primary evidence categories;=20

(c) formal judicial finding based on the unsupported characterisation, with=
 contemporaneous knowledge that the asserted characterisation has no foundat=
ion in the source categories; and=20

(d) publication of the resulting judgment in the National Archives.=20

=20

The total financial consequence of the Para 64 "obsession" framing across t=
he first two judgments is =C2=A31,055,654.50.

=20

Criminal referrals are complex matters. I am seeking legal representation i=
n respect of the matters documented in this analysis.

=20

This document is published on my public archive at https://github.com/nadia=
zahmoul/Zahmoul-v-SSJ-HMCTS-Public-Archive and is distributed to the institu=
tional recipients on the established public-record list.

=20

Yours faithfully,

=20

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

nadia@rosekross.com

+44 (0)7913 328 615

